OK, so we all know what scrolls of earth do.  This YANI is for a wand
to cause the same effect at range.

Zapping the wand would prompt the question "Where?" and the player
would target a square which is within range of the wand (say, 6
squares maximum) in a normal zapping direction (cardinal or diagonal
direction) and within sight.

The effect would be to drop boulders from the ceiling in a 3x3 grid
centred on the square zapped-to.  A blessed wand would do no more than
an uncursed, but a cursed wand would malfunction by hitting a *random*
square within sight.

Zapping the wand whilst swallowed or engulfed, or in a pit or
underwater, would negate the choice of direction (since the player
would not be able to see a target square) and would thus render
effects identical to reading a scroll of earth in such circumstances.

Engraving with the wand would cause dust to sprinkle from the ceiling
overhead and obscure some of the writing.  Breaking the wand, or an
explosion of the wand from bad recharging, would have the same effect
as a cursed scroll of earth, ie, heavy boulders fall right on top of
you.

Such a weapon would be fairly powerful, on a par with cold or fire or
lightning, so the value should be 175 but perhaps a lower probability
than those wands.

